<title>SINGAPORE: Mobil Singapore restarts 45,000-bpd crude unit.</title>
<headline>Mobil Singapore restarts 45,000-bpd crude unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Singapore, a unit of Mobil Corp of the U.S., restarted its 45,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude distillation unit (CDU) over the weekend after being shutdown last week due to technical problems, an industry source said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The source said the unit was back to full capacity after repairs were carried out.</p>
<p>The unit is one of the Mobil's smaller CDUs at its 280,000-bpd refinery at Jurong on the west coast of Singapore.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
